{"ts": 1784366547.070457, "event": "finish", "summary": "Held the entire window (t=0 to t=37m). This was never a wrong-direction entry: price went favorable almost immediately (+55pts by t=1m) and kept making new highs throughout (peaking near +175pts around t=25m), ending the visible window at +167.75pts. Pullbacks were frequent (giveback often 30-90% of the local leg amplitude) but price never approached zero/adverse territory, so each dip read as normal chop within an intact uptrend rather than a reversal. Next time I'd watch for a close that actually crosses back toward 0 or a sustained lower-high/lower-low sequence relative to entry -- neither ever showed up here, which is why HOLD was correct throughout.", "exit_frame": null, "n_commits": 38}
